---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base
	title="School and college ceramics departments"
	description="Manage wheel bookings between classes, kiln firing queues and semester courses with Kilnbook for school and college ceramics departments."
>
	<section class="band-dark page-hero">
		<div class="wrap split">
			<div>
				<p class="eyebrow">Schools &amp; colleges</p>
				<h1>Make room for clay between classes.</h1>
				<p class="lede">
					One or two kilns, a semester timetable and students looking for a wheel between
					classes. Bring bookings, firing queues and courses together with Kilnbook.
				</p>
				<a href="/contact" class="btn">Book a demo</a>
			</div>
			<img
				src="/images/wheel-grid.svg"
				alt="A day view of four wheels reserved in one-hour blocks"
				width="480"
				height="300"
			/>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="wrap section narrow">
		<h2>Wheel time between lectures</h2>
		<p>
			Give students a way to reserve a wheel for independent practice between classes.
			Kilnbook supports one-hour bookings for wheels and hand-building tables, with limits on
			hours and how far ahead members can book. Shared equipment gets its own calendar too.
			<a href="/features/wheel-time">Explore wheel and table booking</a>.
		</p>

		<h2>Keep both kilns' queues in view</h2>
		<p>
			When end-of-semester work starts filling the shelves, see how full each bisque or glaze
			load is and move pieces between loads. Each kiln has its own queue and a firing log with
			the date, cone, schedule and who loaded it. Pickup texts let students know when their work
			is out of the kiln. <a href="/features/firings">See how firings work</a>.
		</p>

		<h2>Courses for the semester, drop-ins for extra practice</h2>
		<p>
			Set up a fixed series of classes for a course, or offer single drop-in sessions alongside
			the semester timetable. Instructors can see their roster, mark attendance and leave notes
			for the next instructor. Waitlists offer cancelled seats to the next student in line.
			<a href="/features/classes">Explore classes and packs</a>.
		</p>

		<h2>A plan for a small kiln room</h2>
		<p>
			The Studio plan covers up to 3 kilns and includes wheel and table reservations, unlimited
			members, class packs and waitlists. That covers a department with one or two kilns, with
			room for a third. <a href="/pricing">Compare plans and limits</a>.
		</p>
	</section>

	<section class="wrap section narrow">
		<h2>Questions departments ask</h2>
		<details>
			<summary>Which plan fits a department with two kilns?</summary>
			<p>
				Studio covers up to 3 kilns and includes wheel and table reservations. Starter covers
				one kiln; Collective covers unlimited kilns. See <a href="/pricing">pricing</a> for
				the full plan details.
			</p>
		</details>
		<details>
			<summary>Can students book wheels between classes?</summary>
			<p>
				Yes. Students can reserve wheels in one-hour blocks. You decide how many hours each
				membership tier gets and how far ahead they can book, so you can set limits for
				independent practice.
			</p>
		</details>
		<details>
			<summary>Do school ceramics programs get a discount?</summary>
			<p>
				School ceramics programs get 30% off any plan. Mention your program when you book a
				demo, as described on the <a href="/pricing">pricing page</a>.
			</p>
		</details>
	</section>

	<section class="cta-band">
		<div class="wrap">
			<h2>Talk through your next semester.</h2>
			<p>Bring your timetable, wheel setup and kiln count to a demo.</p>
			<a href="/contact" class="btn btn-dark">Book a demo</a>
		</div>
	</section>
</Base>
